# Default: let git normalise text in the repo, check out native on the host.
* text=auto

# Anything read or executed inside a Linux container must keep LF: a script
# checked out with CRLF dies with "bad interpreter", and gofmt over a CRLF
# checkout reports every file as unformatted, which makes the CI gate
# impossible to reproduce on a Windows host.
*.go text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf

# Vendored upstream UI assets (ui/upstream/assets): byte-for-byte copies of
# awesome-node-auth's src/ui/assets at cc01e997, pinned by sha256 in
# ui_upstream.go and re-hashed by TestVendoredUIAssetsHaveNotDrifted.
#
# The reference publishes them with LF and ships no .gitattributes of its own,
# so on a host with core.autocrlf=true an unpinned checkout rewrites every line
# of all fourteen: login.html becomes 7198 bytes hashing to facd1ced... where
# the blob the reference actually serves is 7064 bytes hashing to f22f3a3d...
# That is a drift failure on a tree nobody edited, and — worse, if it were ever
# normalised into the table — a permanent pin on bytes no upstream consumer has.
# Hold these paths at LF on every host, in the blob and in the working tree.
ui/upstream/assets/** text eol=lf
